Git Configuration and Commit (配置与提交)
配置 Git
Before using Git, we set up our identity:
```bash
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
#Sets your name for all commits.
git config --global user.email "your.email@example.com"
#Sets your email for all commits.
git config --list
#Shows all current Git settings.

What Is a Commit?
A commit is a snapshot of your project at a specific moment.

Why clear commit messages matter:
 Helps your future self understand what you did
 Helps team members know why changes were made
 Makes debugging easier

Good commit message example:
Add login feature for users
Bad example:
update

Today's Git Workflow
```bash
git config --global user.name "itsladykerrtoo"
git config --global user.email "itsladykerrtoo@email.com"
mkdir git-practice
cd git-practice
git init
echo "# My Git Practice" > README.md
git status
git add README.md
git status
git commit -m "Add README.md with project title"
git log --oneline
